---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import {renderMarkdown} from '../lib/markdown';
import {repositoryUrl} from '../lib/content';
const snippet=await renderMarkdown('```sh\ngit clone https://github.com/ouncebrew/ounce-devkit.git\ncd ounce-devkit\nsh install.sh 20261114\nmake -C examples/vulkan-clear\n```');
const headings=[{text:'Start with a native build',slug:'start-with-a-native-build',depth:2},{text:'Find your next step',slug:'find-your-next-step',depth:2},{text:'The development stack',slug:'the-development-stack',depth:2},{text:'Use the docs in your tools',slug:'use-the-docs-in-your-tools',depth:2}];
---
<DocsLayout title="Documentation" description="A practical development reference for native Switch 2 homebrew with kaiHEN, libounce, OunceVK and ounce-devkit." home headings={headings}>
  <div class="home-intro"><h1>Build native Switch&nbsp;2 homebrew.</h1><p class="lead">A practical reference for kaiHEN application development, from your first NRO to graphics, JIT, and resident services.</p><p class="intro-detail">Understand the runtime. Build with the right libraries. Keep source versions and verification scope close to the code.</p><div class="intro-actions"><a class="button-primary" href="/docs/quickstart/">Start building <Icon name="arrow" size={17}/></a><a class="text-action" href="/docs/api-reference/">Explore the API reference <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></div></div>
  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="start-with-a-native-build"><h2 id="start-with-a-native-build">Start with a native build</h2><p>Install the Switch 2 overlay on devkitPro, then build a small reference application. The Vulkan clear example gives you a focused first test of the native graphics path.</p><div set:html={snippet}/><div class="baseline-note"><strong>Reference baseline</strong><span>ounce-devkit <code>20261114</code> · kaiHEN <code>20261114c</code></span><a href="/docs/quickstart/">Prerequisites and full setup <Icon name="arrow" size={15}/></a></div></section>
  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="find-your-next-step"><h2 id="find-your-next-step">Find your next step</h2><div class="guide-directory"><a href="/docs/first-application/"><strong>Your first application <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></strong><span>Native entry, HEN status, input, and a clean exit.</span></a><a href="/docs/graphics/"><strong>Graphics and UI <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></strong><span>Vulkan, OpenGL ES, presentation, and resolution.</span></a><a href="/docs/jit/"><strong>JIT and runtimes <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></strong><span>Staging, publication, code caches, and emulation.</span></a><a href="/docs/plugins/"><strong>Plugins and IPC <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></strong><span>Resident services, discovery, and resource ownership.</span></a><a href="/docs/porting/"><strong>Port an existing app <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></strong><span>Library selection, platform boundaries, and case studies.</span></a><a href="/docs/debugging/"><strong>Debug and verify <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></strong><span>Trace failures and test a complete application lifecycle.</span></a></div></section>
  <section class="home-section" aria-labelledby="the-development-stack"><h2 id="the-development-stack">The development stack</h2><p>Each layer has a different job. Knowing which one owns a failure makes a port easier to debug.</p><dl class="stack-list"><div><dt>kaiHEN</dt><dd>The resident environment and service interfaces that support native homebrew.</dd></div><div><dt>libounce</dt><dd>The libnx-compatible runtime and platform wrappers for Switch 2.</dd></div><div><dt>OunceVK</dt><dd>Native Vulkan, with EGL and OpenGL through Mesa's Zink.</dd></div><div><dt>ounce-devkit</dt><dd>The libraries, rules, toolchain overlay, and examples for your builds.</dd></div></dl><a class="text-action" href="/docs/runtime/">Understand the runtime architecture <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></section>
  <section class="home-section mcp-section" aria-labelledby="use-the-docs-in-your-tools"><Icon name="plug" size={23}/><h2 id="use-the-docs-in-your-tools">Use the docs in your tools</h2><p>Search and retrieve these same guides through a read-only MCP endpoint. Responses include section links, source references, and research dates.</p><div class="endpoint-line"><code>https://kaihen.timsfun.com/mcp</code><button type="button" class="copy-endpoint" aria-label="Copy MCP endpoint"><Icon name="copy" size={17}/><span>Copy</span></button></div><a class="text-action" href="/docs/mcp/">Connection guide and available tools <Icon name="arrow" size={16}/></a></section>
  <div class="evidence-note"><strong>Read the evidence with the guide.</strong><p>This reference is based on the November 13, 2026 research snapshot. Source declarations, build checks, and console tests establish different things. <a href="/docs/sources/">See sources and verification scope.</a></p></div>
  <footer class="article-footer"><span>Independent developer documentation</span><a href={repositoryUrl}>Source on GitHub</a><a href="/downloads/kaihen-docs-2026-11-14.zip" download>Download the documentation</a></footer>
</DocsLayout>
